{
  "book": "2KI",
  "chapter": 2,
  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-1d43ef69af728c64": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-328",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "In India the expression “bald-head” has no special reference to a lack of hair, but is often applied to men who have an abundance. It is rather a term of contempt, intended to signify a mean and worthless fellow. The Hebrews valued a good head of hair and greatly deprecated baldn…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-328",
          "sourceHash": "626a182240987e98dcbc7c76b597a4b5ee7d0c55d3d00d5c2ef7ad5ada1604d8",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-446e720d2e368fb8": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-326",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The disciples of the prophets were called sons, as teachers are sometimes called fathers (2 Kings 2:12; 6:21). These “sons of the prophets” formed a peculiar order, whose mission seems to have been to assist the prophet in their duties, and in time to succeed them. They were not…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-326",
          "sourceHash": "3dc7c9cecbf7f979442a04e504ee25611f88a6dbd9cb558a87d79b51ae57c891",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-698df07733e04e0a": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-327",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "Tselochith, here translated “cruse,” is rendered “dish” in 2 Kings 21:13 “pan,” in 2 Chronicles 35:13 and “bosom” in Proverbs 19:24; 26:15. It is supposed to have been a flat metal dish.",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-327",
          "sourceHash": "0e943ed2e3ca573d3b40549256c9bec93289aeb5b9c5ee777eaff50b323322c5",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
